# `each k:[3 6] j:[12 22]` fans one file out into the four combinations, 48x48 PNGs each_matrix_3_12.png,
# each_matrix_3_22.png, each_matrix_6_12.png, each_matrix_6_22.png, with {k} and {j} in the path. Each shows one red
# regular polygon with an ink outline centered at (24,24): k is the side count and j is the radius.
# each_matrix_3_12: a small triangle, circumradius 12. each_matrix_3_22: a large triangle, circumradius 22.
# each_matrix_6_12: a small hexagon, circumradius 12. each_matrix_6_22: a large hexagon, circumradius 22.
@artboard 48x48
@target targets/each_matrix_{k}_{j}.png each k:[3 6] j:[12 22]

poly k r:j at:24,24 fill:p.red stroke:p.ink,2
